<title>AUSTRIA: BOBSLEIGH-WORLD CUP FOUR-MAN RESULTS.</title>
<headline>BOBSLEIGH-WORLD CUP FOUR-MAN RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>IGLS, Austria 1996-12-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of a World Cup</p>
<p>four-man bobsleigh event on Sunday:</p>
<p>1. Germany 2 (Dirk Wiese, Christoph Bartsch, Kai Uwe</p>
<p>    Kohlert, Michael Liekmeier)   1:43.37 (51.47, 51.90)</p>
<p>2. Switzerland 1 (Marcel Rohner, Markus Nuessli, Thomas</p>
<p>    Schreiber, Roland Tanner)     1:43.41 (51.47, 51.94)</p>
<p>3. Germany I (Wolfgang Hoppe, Sven Ruehr, Oliver</p>
<p>    Felsen, Carsten Embach)	 1:43.42 (51.51, 51.91)</p>
<p>4. Austria I (Hubert Schoesser, Gerd Habermueller,</p>
<p>Erwin Arnold, Martin Schuetzenauer) 1:43.69</p>
<p>(51.69, 52.00)</p>
<p>5. Switzerland III (Christian Reich, Steve Anderhub,</p>
<p>Roger Graber, Thomas Handschin) 1:43.71</p>
<p>(51.67, 52.04)</p>
<p>6 equal. Switzerland II (Reto Goetschi, Guido Acklin,</p>
<p>   Daniel Giger, Beat Saitz)	1:43.74 (51.66, 52.08)</p>
<p>6 equal. United States I (Brian Shimer, Chip Minton,</p>
<p>   Randy Jones, Robert Olesen)    1:43.74 51.65, 52.09)</p>
<p>8. Germany III (Harald Czudaj, Torsten Voss, Alexander</p>
<p>    Szelig, Udo Lehmann)	    1:43.91 (51.79, 52.12)</p>
<p>9. United States II (Jim Herberich, Jason Dorsey,</p>
<p>    Garrett Hines, John Kasper)   1:43.96 (51.94, 52.02)</p>
<p>10. Italy I (Guenther Huber, Antonio Tartaglia,</p>
<p>Massimiliano Roter, Marco Menchini) 1:44.01 (51.83,</p>
<p>52.18).</p>
